WEBVTT

00:00.950 --> 00:05.350
Interview preparation shouldn't begin
two weeks before the interview.

00:10.950 --> 00:13.400
Choose the role and your career stage.

00:13.800 --> 00:16.300
Add your resume and the job description.

00:16.650 --> 00:18.700
The interview is built from them.

00:19.950 --> 00:21.300
The interviewer asks.

00:21.900 --> 00:25.600
You answer out loud, and your words
appear as you speak.

00:26.200 --> 00:30.400
When an answer has no result,
it asks a sharper follow-up.

00:36.950 --> 00:39.850
Each answer is scored on five vectors:

00:40.200 --> 00:45.200
structure, domain, strategy,
communication, and leadership.

00:45.700 --> 00:51.100
Situation, task, action, and result
are checked in every answer.

00:53.450 --> 00:56.650
The report opens with an
executive interpretation.

00:57.100 --> 00:58.750
Your strongest signal.

00:59.150 --> 01:00.750
Your development focus.

01:01.200 --> 01:03.300
Evidence from your own answers,

01:03.500 --> 01:06.700
and a thirty, sixty, ninety day plan.

01:07.100 --> 01:08.850
Download it as a PDF.

01:10.050 --> 01:11.900
Every session is saved.

01:12.350 --> 01:16.300
Compare sessions, and see how
your scores move over time.

01:21.450 --> 01:24.800
Practice. Polish. Place.
